# Relayout Button

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

`method: "relayout"` updates layout properties (title, axis ranges, background,
annotations, etc.) without touching trace data. **Light** restores the light
appearance while keeping the current zoom; **Reset** restores both the light
appearance and automatic axis ranges.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

xs = Enum.to_list(1..20)
ys = Enum.map(xs, fn x -> :math.sin(x / 3.0) * x / 10 end)

light = %{plot_bgcolor: "white", paper_bgcolor: "white", font: %{color: "#444"}}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(Scatter.new(x: xs, y: ys, mode: "lines+markers"))
|> Figure.update_layout(light)
|> Figure.update_layout(
  title: %{text: "Relayout Button Examples"},
  xaxis: %{title: %{text: "x"}},
  yaxis: %{title: %{text: "y"}},
  updatemenus: [%{
    type: "buttons",
    direction: "right",
    x: 0.5,
    xanchor: "center",
    y: 1.12,
    buttons: [
      %{label: "Light",
        method: "relayout",
        args: [light]},
      %{label: "Dark",
        method: "relayout",
        args: [%{plot_bgcolor: "#1a1a2e", paper_bgcolor: "#16213e",
                 font: %{color: "white"}}]},
      %{label: "Zoom In",
        method: "relayout",
        args: [%{"xaxis.range": [5, 15], "yaxis.range": [-1, 1]}]},
      %{label: "Reset",
        method: "relayout",
        args: [Map.merge(light, %{"xaxis.autorange": true, "yaxis.autorange": true})]}
    ]
  }]
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
